-- title:
--   Stabilisation of the chain P^m M on Eisenstein-quotient rational points
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and write $J_0(p)$ for `JZero p`, the degree-zero Picard group of the level-$p$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, equipped with the module structure `heckeModuleBar p` over the Hecke algebra $\mathbb T=$ `HeckeAlg` $=\mathbb Z[X_\ell:\ell\ \text{prime}]$, in which the variable at $\ell$ acts by `heckeOperatorBar p ℓ`; the hypothesis `hcomm` says that these operators commute pairwise. Let $q$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak P=$ `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q` be the preimage, under the $\mathbb Z$-algebra evaluation `eisensteinEval p` at the level-$p$ Eisenstein system, of the ideal $(q)\subseteq\mathbb Z$. Put $\mathfrak a\cdot J_0(p)=$ `eisensteinKernelSubmodule`, the submodule obtained by acting with the ideal `eisensteinKernel (JZero p) (eisensteinIdeal p)` on all of $J_0(p)$, let $\tilde J=J_0(p)/\mathfrak a\cdot J_0(p)$, and let $\tilde J(\mathbb Q)\subseteq\tilde J$ be the image of $\{x\in J_0(p):\sigma\cdot x-x\in\mathfrak a\cdot J_0(p)\ \text{for all}\ \sigma\in\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\}$. Write $M$ for the $\mathbb T$-submodule of $\tilde J$ spanned by $\tilde J(\mathbb Q)$ and $M_{\mathfrak P}$ for its localisation at the complement of $\mathfrak P$. Assume: (i) the additive subgroup generated by $\tilde J(\mathbb Q)$ is a finitely generated abelian group; (ii) for every $m$ a datum `JKummerRow q m` over $M_{\mathfrak P}$ is given, consisting of abelian groups $M_0$, $H^1_{\mathrm{tors}}$, $H^1$, an injective homomorphism $M_0\to M_{\mathfrak P}$ with finite-index image, a homomorphism $\delta:M_0\to H^1_{\mathrm{tors}}$ whose kernel is exactly $q^mM_0$, and a homomorphism $H^1_{\mathrm{tors}}\to H^1$ making the pair exact at $H^1_{\mathrm{tors}}$ and having image the $q^m$-torsion of $H^1$; (iii) there is $c_0>0$ with $[\,M_{\mathfrak P}:q^mM_{\mathfrak P}\,]\le c_0\cdot\#H^1_{\mathrm{tors}}(m)$ for all $m$; and (iv) the cardinalities $\#H^1_{\mathrm{tors}}(m)$ are bounded by a single constant. The conclusion is that the decreasing chain of submodules $\mathfrak P^mM$ stabilises: there exists $m_0$ such that $\mathfrak P^mM=\mathfrak P^{m_0}M$ for every $m\ge m_0$.
--
--   This is the stabilisation step in Mazur's analysis of the Eisenstein ideal: bounded Kummer-theoretic data at all $q$-power levels force the $\mathfrak P$-adic filtration of the Hecke-module generated by the rational points of the Eisenstein quotient to become constant. It is used to deduce that those rational points are torsion, in [`ModularCurve.eisensteinQuotientRational_isTorsion_heckeModuleBar`](thm.html#ModularCurve.eisensteinQuotientRational_isTorsion_heckeModuleBar).
